{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>A dwelling house of a walled city.</b> Since the city is surrounded by a wall, the ground of the house is never used for sowing, and the Holy One, blessed be He, did not decree return in the Jubilee except for land upon which human life depends. Another interpretation: ordinarily, one who buys a house in a walled city buys it permanently, for in another's house a person is not inclined to settle comfortably and to build any structure in it; therefore it is written of it, 'it shall not go out in the Jubilee.' But a field and courtyard houses, which a person is accustomed to take as sharecropping and leasing, it is written of them that they go out in the Jubilee." "<b>The year of its sale.</b> And not from the count of the world (i.e., not counted from Creation)." "<b>Days.</b> A year, that is, until the return of the days of the sun to their place."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:15.952132182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}